{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "family_id": "machine.i915fake",
  "summary": "The i915 driver on the fake chip in QEMU: under the GNU root the identity libdrm reads, the driver Mesa's loader picks and the faults of the chip's debugfs file, which tests/cases/machine/i915fake_scenario.c runs; under the test image the buffers i915gemprobe tiles, maps and reads back",
  "cases": [
    {
      "case_id": "machine.i915fake.crocus",
      "behavior": "with rach2.i915fake the i915 driver binds QEMU's edu device with the fake chip behind it: drmdevice reports 8086:0a16 on board 17aa:380c, Mesa's loader under eglinfo's surfaceless platform picks crocus for it, and first light run from the fake's debugfs file passes, fails by name under each fault armed there, and passes again once the fault is spent",
      "units": [
        "rach2/sys/drm/i915/i915_fake.c",
        "drmdevice",
        "eglinfo"
      ],
      "domain": "machine",
      "architectures": [
        "x86_64"
      ],
      "workload": {
        "arguments": [],
        "inputs": {},
        "repetitions": 1,
        "seed": null
      },
